\subsection{Peak-period to zero-crossing-period bridge}
\label{sec:sea3-tp-tz-bridge}

The spectral sea family above is parameterized by the physically conventional
peak periods $T_{p,r}$, but the deployed tuner does \emph{not} estimate a peak
period.  Its canonical period state is the zero-crossing/moment period
$T_z$ produced by \texttt{WavePeriodEstimator}.  These quantities must therefore
remain distinct in the certificate.

For a scalar spectrum $\Phi(\omega)$ with angular-frequency moments
\begin{equation}
 m_j[\Phi]:=\int_0^\infty \omega^j\Phi(\omega)\,d\omega,
 \label{eq:sea3-spectral-moments}
\end{equation}
the corresponding ideal zero-crossing period is
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{T_z[\Phi]=2\pi\sqrt{\frac{m_0[\Phi]}{m_2[\Phi]}}.}
 \label{eq:sea3-tz-moment}
\end{equation}
For a multimodal sea the spectral moments add before this ratio is formed;
periods are not averaged independently.  Consequently two partitions with the
same $T_p$ but different $\gamma$, energy share, direction, or vessel response
need not induce the same tuner period.

SEA0 must therefore certify a relation
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 (\lambda,x^s)\in\widehat{\mathcal S}_{\rm SEA3}
 \Longrightarrow
 T_z^{\rm src}\in\mathcal T_z(\lambda,x^s),
 }
 \label{eq:sea3-tp-tz-relation}
\end{equation}
using the same directional response of
Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-matrix-spectrum} and the exact deployed
WavePeriodEstimator front end.  For an analytical spectral enclosure,
Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-tz-moment} supplies the moment bridge; for the final source
certificate the leaky filters, finite EMAs, log-period state, initialization,
and clamps are propagated explicitly.  Thus a bound on $T_{p,r}$ alone is never
substituted for a bound on the tuner state.

The same qualification is essential for acceleration variance.  The ideal
JONSWAP high-frequency elevation tail is proportional to $\omega^{-5}$, whereas
specific acceleration multiplies elevation power by $\omega^4$.  An unbounded
idealized acceleration second moment would therefore contain an asymptotic
$\int d\omega/\omega$ term and is not a finite certificate quantity.  The
heuristic scaling $\sigma_{a}T_p^2/H_s=O(1)$ becomes usable only after the
certified vessel/IMU response and the deployed finite wave band are included.
SEA0 must bound that response-weighted, band-limited statistic; it must not use
an unbanded JONSWAP acceleration variance as a theorem assumption.

The $0.03$--$1.2$ Hz numbers quoted in the screening estimates are therefore
bounds on the \emph{committed tuning-frequency channel}, not an asserted
$T_p$ range for the physical sea.  The SEA3 P2 refinement may use a tighter
$T_z/T_p$ relation only after SEA0 has certified it over the declared
JONSWAP/PM mixture and directional response family.  This certified bridge is
a SEA0 promotion gate, not an optional tightening of the later P2/P3 search.
